# The annotations of tape block 2, the BASIC program "TUJAD" at PROG $5CCB-$5D22 (88 bytes): the source of
# src/tape/basic.asm and src/tape/basic/*.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/tape/basic.json). Format:
# ../../../../docs/ann-format.md. Witness: c1 (work/stage1/c1: power-on, the tape at ROM speed), whose ROM LOADs
# this block and runs its line 10 (docs/03-build-and-load.md 3.2; tools/basic_list.py work/stage1/blocks/basic.bin).

@module basic ; The BASIC: line 10, which clears the screen black, loads the CODE block and calls its stub
@about Tape block 2 holds the program "TUJAD" (header: LINE 10, program length 88, no variables). The one line is CLEAR 24767: PAPER 0: INK 0: POKE 23624,0: CLS : LOAD "" CODE 16384: RANDOMIZE USR 23296. Every number is its digits, then the number marker $0E and the five-byte small-integer form the ROM reads.
@about c1: the ROM loads the block at signal speed and runs the line at once (LINE 10); the stub at $5B00 is entered at frame 2908, T 8352 (WALKTHROUGH 1).

$5CCB b BasicLine10 ; BASIC line 10: CLEAR 24767: PAPER 0: INK 0: POKE 23624,0: CLS : LOAD "" CODE 16384: RANDOMIZE USR 23296
> The whole program (the header's program length 88 covers it all): the line number 10 (two bytes, high byte first), the line's length (84, low byte first), then seven statements split by ":" ($3A) and closed by ENTER ($0D).
> CLEAR 24767 puts RAMTOP at $60BF, one byte below the game block (GameStart $60C0, src/game). PAPER 0 and INK 0 make the next CLS black on black, POKE 23624,0 sets BORDCR (a black border and a black lower screen), so the picture loads into a black screen. LOAD "" CODE 16384 loads the next file, tape blocks 3 and 4, at $4000 (the header's own start, 32768, is overridden): the loading screen and the 32-byte stub at $5B00. RANDOMIZE USR 23296 calls the stub (StubLoad $5B00 in src/screen), which never returns.
$5CCD ; the line's length, 84
$5CCF ; CLEAR ($FD) "24767"
$5CD5 ; $0E and 24767 = $60BF as a small integer (0, 0, low, high, 0)
$5CDB ; ":" PAPER ($DA) "0"
$5CDE ; $0E and 0
$5CE4 ; ":" INK ($D9) "0"
$5CE7 ; $0E and 0
$5CED ; ":" POKE ($F4) "23624"
$5CF4 ; $0E and 23624 = $5C48 (BORDCR), then "," and "0"
$5CFC ; $0E and 0
$5D02 ; ":" CLS ($FB)
$5D04 ; ":" LOAD ($EF) "" CODE ($AF) "16384"
$5D0E ; $0E and 16384 = $4000
$5D14 ; ":" RANDOMIZE ($F9) USR ($C0) "23296"
$5D1C ; $0E and 23296 = $5B00
$5D22 ; ENTER
